      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The source places an attributed Pythagorean view of Number as an organizing principle beside an explicit question about how far numerical thought has progressed, then counters closure expectations with a concessive picture: number theory's venerability, power, beauty, and established truths are compatible with infancy and continuing discovery, because discoveries produce further questions, guesses, heuristics, expectations, and problems.",
